# IYDT-GSRP optical-crater MultiPEM analyses

These two-stage rapid assessments combine optical and crater observations to
infer SUGAR log-yield and HOB. The EIV case infers selected benchmark yields;
the other fixes benchmark yields at their supplied values.

| Directory | Benchmark-yield treatment |
| --- | --- |
| `I-EIV-SUGAR-hob-0` | errors in variables |
| `I-SUGAR-hob-0` | fixed |

## Native prerequisites

```text
ln -s ../../../Applications/Code/IYDT-gsrp/Phenomenology Code
mkdir -p Opt
```

Run the matching single-phenomenology calibrations first and stage their MLE
results:

```text
cp ../Optical/I-EIV-SUGAR-hob-0/opt.RData Opt/opt_1_eiv_0.RData
cp ../Crater/I-EIV-SUGAR-0/opt.RData Opt/opt_2_eiv_0.RData
cp ../Optical/I-SUGAR-hob-0/opt.RData Opt/opt_1_0.RData
cp ../Crater/I-SUGAR-0/opt.RData Opt/opt_2_0.RData
```

The EIV deck reads the two `*_eiv_0.RData` files; the fixed-yield deck reads
the other two. These are required `opt_files_in`, not generated automatically.

Enter the chosen analysis directory, run `runMPEM.r`, wait for successful
calibration, and always preserve its pristine `.RData` separately (for example,
as `.RData-calibration`) for future event analyses. Only then run
`runMPEM_0.r`; run native batch jobs in the background as described in
`../README`.

For Docker, copy the four source files out of their single-phenomenology job
snapshots into the canonical `Opt` destinations before creating the dependent
job. Run either analysis by its path under `IYDT-gsrp/2-Phen-oc`.
